   "fix": "Move the query into `mathlib_cache.py` (e.g. `newest_cached_master_commit(gh, repo)`, next to `master_build_published`) and have `cached_master_tip` call it with the module-level `gh`, exactly as `cache_published` does.",
   "issue": "`GitHub.cached_master_tip` builds its own `build.yml/runs?branch=master&event=push&status=success` query, duplicating the mathlib-cache policy that `scripts/mathlib_cache.py` declares it owns (\"the one definition for every script\"); the immediately following `cache_published` (line 162) correctly delegates there. It is also the only entry in `GitHub` that is not a generic git fact. The two spellings already differ (`status=success` vs `status == \"completed\" and conclusion == \"success\"`), and this rev is exempted from the cache check in `resolve` (`m != cached`, line 371), so drift here directly decides whether an uncached rev is proposed.",
   "line": 157
  }
